  "articleBody": "Adding onto your home is a big investment, and nobody wants to throw money away on avoidable mistakes. Here are some common pitfalls and how to steer clear of them: \n\n1. **Underestimating the Schedule:** Home additions typically take much longer than a simple room refresh. *How to avoid it:* Get a realistic timeline from your contractor and factor in potential delays for permits or material lead times. \n\n2. **Not Reserving Contingency Budget:** Unexpected issues can always pop up, especially with structural changes. *How to avoid it:* Always set aside 10-20% of your budget for unforeseen circumstances. \n\n3. **Poor Coordination Among Trades:** When plumbers, electricians, and carpenters aren't working in sync, delays and rework happen. *How to avoid it:* Choose a contractor like HH Remodeling LLC who excels at coordinating all sub-trades, ensuring a smooth workflow. \n\n4. **Failing to Plan for Dependencies:** One step often can't start until another is complete, and missing this can halt progress. *How to avoid it:* A detailed project plan, managed by an experienced general contractor, will map out these dependencies. \n\nBy being aware of these common mistakes and working with a professional who can manage the complexities, you can keep your home addition project on track and on budget.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
